  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR) initiated preparations to discuss an impeachment motion against Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka after 120 members from eight factions formally submitted a proposal. As the legislative body moved toward a plenary session, the Vice President officially resigned from his position, resulting in the immediate cancellation of the scheduled impeachment proceedings. Following the conclusion of this high-stakes political development, the DPR continued its regular legislative schedule, holding plenary meetings to discuss bills related to the formation of laws. Recent sessions saw the attendance of hundreds of members, and images circulated of legislators interacting with Deputy Speaker Dasco following the conclusion of the assembly. These events mark a significant shift in the nation's executive and legislative landscape for the 2026-2027 session, moving from the focus on constitutional impeachment to standard parliamentary activity.",
